// com.journeyapps:zxing-android-embedded:4.3.0 -- the one dependency of
// OpenEUICC that AOSP does not already carry.
//
// Every other entry in OpenEUICC-deps-defaults resolves to an existing AOSP
// module (androidx.core_core-ktx, appcompat, material, constraintlayout,
// preference, lifecycle, swiperefreshlayout, cardview, viewpager2,
// datastore-preferences). This is the only one carrying the OpenEUICC_ prefix,
// which is upstream's convention for "not in AOSP" -- hence the only thing
// standing between us and a working LPA.
//
// It supplies the camera capture wrapper only: ScanContract / ScanOptions in
// app-common's DownloadWizardMethodSelectFragment.kt, and the
// com.journeyapps.barcodescanner.CaptureActivity declared in app-common's
// manifest. The pure-Java half of zxing -- QRCodeReader, RGBLuminanceSource,
// BinaryBitmap, HybridBinarizer, used in Utils.kt to decode a QR out of an
// image file -- comes from external/zxing, already in the tree.
//
// Its POM declares exactly one dependency, com.google.zxing:core:3.4.1.
// external/zxing is 3.5.2, which is forward compatible, so zxing-core covers
// it and no second prebuilt is needed.
//
// Apache 2.0, so shipping the binary unmodified is fine and carries no source
// obligation of its own. OpenEUICC itself is GPLv3 and stays unmodified, which
// is the reason to vendor this AAR rather than patch the QR scanner out.
//
// sdk_version is deliberately unset. zxing-core is a platform module (no
// sdk_version), and a module declaring sdk_version cannot depend on a platform
// one; leaving it unset makes this a platform module too, matching
// OpenEUICC-common.
//
// sha256 of the AAR as fetched from repo1.maven.org:
//   4ab03353127c34e55cbb80fbc9a34031decbcfb1ec5e8f991944d2d494621a33

android_library_import {
    name: "OpenEUICC_com.journeyapps_zxing-android-embedded",
    aars: ["zxing-android-embedded-4.3.0.aar"],
    static_libs: [
        "zxing-core",
        "androidx.appcompat_appcompat",
        "androidx.core_core",
    ],
    system_ext_specific: true,
}
